# ByteForce SEO Strategy

## Primary business objective

SEO exists to generate qualified software-development leads for ByteForce.

The primary conversion is:

/contact

Optimize for qualified leads, not traffic volume.

## Positioning

ByteForce is a custom software engineering company.

Primary positioning:

- custom software development
- web applications
- SaaS development
- CRM development
- ERP development
- business software
- workflow automation
- API/integration work
- application modernization

Do not position ByteForce as a generic low-cost web agency.

## Target markets

Primary:
- Morocco
- Casablanca

Secondary:
- France
- French-speaking businesses

## Commercial SEO principle

Prioritize keywords where the searcher could realistically hire ByteForce.

Commercial intent > informational traffic.

A page targeting 50 highly relevant searches is potentially more valuable
than a page targeting thousands of generic informational searches.

## Page architecture

One primary intent per URL. The public tree is the allowlist in `lib/money/index.ts`.

Software:

- `/developpement-logiciel-sur-mesure-maroc`
- CRM, then remplacer Excel and CRM personnalisé
- ERP, then ERP personnalisé and logiciel de gestion
- logiciel métier
- automatisation
- `/application-web-sur-mesure-maroc`
- `/developpement-saas-maroc`
- `/developpement-application-mobile-maroc`

Problems: `/solutions/remplacer-excel`, `/solutions/remplacer-saas`, `/solutions/automatisation-entreprise`, `/solutions/moderniser-application`

Audiences: `/solutions/logiciel-pme`, `/solutions/logiciel-entreprise`

Locations: `/developpement-logiciel-casablanca`, `/developpement-logiciel-france`

Case studies stay on `/realisations`. Do not invent YourSmile. Company pages stay `/a-propos` and `/contact`.

Do not add a child URL that this tree does not name. Retired URLs redirect in `next.config.ts`.

`/taches` is the internal board. It stays noindex.

## Content rules

Every SEO page must:

1. Target one primary search intent.
2. Have one clear H1.
3. Use natural semantic keyword coverage.
4. Explain a real business problem.
5. Explain how ByteForce solves it.
6. Include relevant use cases.
7. Include process information.
8. Include genuine ByteForce proof when available.
9. Include useful FAQs.
10. Link to relevant commercial pages.
11. Link to /contact.
12. Have a strong conversion CTA.
13. Have unique title and meta description.
14. Have appropriate structured data.
15. Avoid keyword stuffing.
16. Avoid generic AI-generated filler.
17. Never invent clients, results, statistics, testimonials or case studies.

## Conversion

Every commercial page must eventually answer:

"Why should this company contact ByteForce?"

Primary CTA:

Parler de mon projet

Secondary CTA may be contextual:

- Construire mon SaaS
- Créer mon CRM sur mesure
- Automatiser mon processus
- Évaluer le sur-mesure
- Discuter de mon projet

All CTAs ultimately point to /contact.

## Design

Do NOT redesign ByteForce simply to implement SEO.

Use the existing ByteForce design system.

SEO content must feel like premium software engineering
company content, not an SEO content farm.

Avoid:

- huge walls of text
- repetitive cards
- artificial keyword sections
- generic stock-agency language
- "In today's digital world..."
- meaningless statistics
- excessive gradients
- AI-looking layouts

## Technical SEO

For every new page verify:

- canonical
- title
- meta description
- Open Graph
- robots directives
- sitemap inclusion
- semantic HTML
- H1/H2 hierarchy
- internal links
- image alt text
- JSON-LD where appropriate
- Core Web Vitals
- mobile rendering
- indexability
- no duplicate intent/cannibalization

## Internal linking

Money pages should link to related problem pages,
case studies and /contact.

Problem pages should link back to the relevant money page.

Case studies should link to the service that was actually delivered.

Do not create orphan pages.

## Before creating a new SEO page

First determine:

1. Primary keyword
2. Search intent
3. Existing ByteForce page that could already satisfy it
4. Cannibalization risk
5. Related pages
6. Internal-link opportunities
7. Conversion goal

If an existing page already satisfies the intent,
improve that page instead of creating another URL.
